Ethical and Legal Requirements
[label=(0)]
The mitigation strategy must be ethically justifiable {{cite:d34667024c03742879a28ca2e4f15d414923da59}}

The measures should be necessary, proportionate, legitimate, just, scientifically valid, and time-bound {{cite:d34667024c03742879a28ca2e4f15d414923da59}}, {{cite:4342eca8be1bf15dd386fafb16ed66f892bf0301}}, {{cite:d85ff046091ee9fd680d39f1fc23a7d8e98409ad}}, {{cite:9cdd16f67e8c075af0c566ab100753cf9c2fe141}}, {{cite:ebaeed78e0e164511f038d779863609d35c2c280}}

They should not be invasive {{cite:0b0c0f3e60991167ba3fc7ef2a1f3d66a9b1468d}} and must not be done at the expense of individual civil rights {{cite:861a2369c0e75a35755eb7a1b477ded56e4eebe4}}, {{cite:c236f14430b0c556b2cd4cd47ea91c0fc59539f8}}, {{cite:ebaeed78e0e164511f038d779863609d35c2c280}}

Means of protection should be available to anyone {{cite:d34667024c03742879a28ca2e4f15d414923da59}}

They should be voluntary {{cite:c236f14430b0c556b2cd4cd47ea91c0fc59539f8}}, {{cite:dbdd344d84be24d05d0416dad0e24585380b9908}}

The measures must comply with legal regulations {{cite:ebaeed78e0e164511f038d779863609d35c2c280}}, {{cite:59c4c81fa1038e87211df91a3189d8a534d26a03}}, {{cite:87c1d4d6ce407abe2b145be414f830362981ab92}}

