Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) {{cite:15dcc1928ace2fd5107dc6e42b942e3056b30bb0}}
are complex architectures composed of a cascade of multiple
linear and non-linear layers.

In particular, formal verification of ML classifiers started to be
an active field of investigation {{cite:367a61f33b062c3595f96c82101ff9a7c34d6f3d}}, {{cite:ec0d89ad50071ba35209b988d2aa0174b84ab580}}, {{cite:49e992ec6dd4d292a73baa14356e821a7bb20a58}}, {{cite:9edb5bc171acbeccf430876a94607fed589cdc7a}}, {{cite:a768077b208a384232bb8c475a9ef06c02f2d402}}, {{cite:60a317ba52fdaf050196c574bcba87b2043efbbd}}, {{cite:6400cbf5cd74595915a992141a1366536090753e}}, {{cite:f6d6809a298dad262dcd6519eb1a77f171e19fe2}}, {{cite:39ec2f67fbac42703491157f0f2441460d5057f9}}, {{cite:b56eb26eac4ce4a02d2e7f5dc2868640cb318353}}, {{cite:31dac6b5de3a9657a142be5ebb90b9e0a482ea26}}, {{cite:922ebbced6464f1065e8656445a8feef4430c8d2}}, {{cite:1294ab74222675f1c3014642babcf69cc5f48aaa}}
within the verification and static analysis community.

For example, in Optics we find models based on the Poynting vector and
the Maxwell equations already in the 1950s,{{cite:a85e27713f2c20cc69e128ae594023b3529f0a43}}, {{cite:cfb949971019e707f758363a7e1067783ccc828a}}
and only much later the approaches of Bohm and Madelung were
considered.{{cite:712577af86e6db9d1e9bb1c1623a35ce2a4695aa}}, {{cite:1cec9d29f732e9b9fb6ea03d886039e9c7ad98f6}}, {{cite:6282caacc923c19650930ab780a8c563961cac02}}, {{cite:5bd5ba675e3294f205c139d7d896d07d5c950bb0}}, {{cite:ff6449c1cac4bec361c3b8d95940dd3790b13191}}, {{cite:d2e5408e8966e63f78b9623526e114639e332c76}}, {{cite:3e8c830a1ac120ea24c0f3b37c0efa6729da030e}}, {{cite:2738a03a1acd3bef5160d7eea4afe5d5a7e5565b}}
In Acoustics the use of streamlines was also suggested in the 1980s as
a visualization and analysis tool,{{cite:8078a0ebee9182ea75b11d80c17a913dc18c6b05}}, {{cite:d2a7117b8cdaa228e50109cd3b0ed3c195c001cc}}, {{cite:6a14ce6c27e1148caa1bf01a7e5183e12131b9d5}}, {{cite:91b21fd81b4efb8bdaab3d5701a48822891754bf}}, {{cite:ab9921fe21c36ca6a905253e9ea701e3d699003e}}
although there was not a direct link with Madelung or Bohm in this
direction until recently.{{cite:b9f604a39666809fa4b950694679767b88b6058d}}
Finally, we also find different models aimed at treating dissipation in
quantum systems, such as the one proposed by Kostin,{{cite:df7ef674026abd36c917f35a851ef57da4dc9cf6}}
which is based on the idea of adding nonlinear
contributions to the Schrödinger equation, which, interestingly, are
given in terms of the phase of the wave function, and therefore the
Bohmian momentum (which is identified with the dissipative term that
appears in the classical Newton equations of motion with friction).

