so much research has focused on time series embedding{{cite:2e985692b335ec60a539487285d0063148284c61}}:
Algorithms based on DTW and traditional embedding techniques {{cite:d47adc56be08482800d8e26b41b7f81f41036acd}}
aim to project original time series data into feature-vector space;
Symbolic representations {{cite:7d5ffcf258abeb6b29212251e16239f6b3ae0e8a}}, {{cite:f4c650623ca434dbc5f9a2fe5f88cfaf860d5cec}}, {{cite:8061c5d6520976fdc8b36f308443eea2390edf3f}}
transform time series using symbols such as characters in a given alphabet;
Shapelet discovery-based models {{cite:3cf54e07812b395b22c0da1f432532bc71d6c746}}, {{cite:b4e70491e562470a8b95634ef4f522564d06df18}}, {{cite:f62a5ced70d610a828344cb36668a5ad492a6268}}, {{cite:a40d6b9a650e79c44e124ff5e8f5261695f9802d}}, {{cite:39b6a08be0381b94a13c4402f93880862231fb2c}},
from another perspective, try to find typical subsequences based on certain criteria such as information gain.

