of general position, where every {{formula:3f3a41f9-ea08-443c-915b-75a18e065e8f}}  distinct vectors in {{formula:914b1a1b-b3f2-403e-86c3-d7e1d0ed8902}} 
are linearly independent.

Some methods {{cite:ade155cddb914e8c8fd5dc1cf0ba4f1c34b9032f}}, {{cite:e23617c8b0e70517995975054d95f36515284103}}
employ depth sensing cameras (such as Kinect) {{cite:b3c2141cf81d23d88e67b289c284b906989fbfca}}
to directly measure the variations in the distance between a fixed
surface (such as wall) and the chest-wall.

Simulations are carried out mainly in random-regular networks {{cite:3dd09b46526d2bcf5f1290cabf5f6effc4978554}}, {{cite:77262f5232ac5c5cb2f78409c89dc061acd1904a}}
but, Erdős-Rényi graphs {{cite:2a512597231b3264ea203e948eb42f6521916fe5}}, {{cite:13f6f022fc3a466368528c4a80ff67feff3f8b1a}}
and networks with a power-law degree distribution {{cite:441b5216d590bb8bb1c8d5ac031b6a6fda6a39e1}}, {{cite:f9a53ec36d2ccb3ae9a28af37791c4c6aa374b35}} are also considered.

