More recently, numerous approaches are proposed to improve the adapted segmentation and can be categorized as follows:
1) output space {{cite:b0e8d2e31b8824ee298d43bb22890d5fce108ac0}} and spatial-aware {{cite:7c96c3cd1ccc771b4fff14d7c969d24b4e9622da}} adaptations aim to align the global structure (e.g., scene layout) across domains;
2) pixel-level adaptation synthesizes target samples {{cite:3eb534463066100b28786272f795c171a6f8a16a}}, {{cite:033bef776b8afa1b261bece209f8e52b58ef0191}}, {{cite:ba0aa6a8aca5c71dee087555afdb4523a8868789}}, {{cite:58af0f098b54c3d4b8d5ddd69268321c11f86398}} to reduce the domain gap during training the segmentation model;
3) pseudo label re-training {{cite:1c4f5b3b992d412bb89085db640d770b40eb37ae}}, {{cite:97e119fbe86b7b3254f08cb6b101580c5193eb13}} generates pseudo ground truth of target images to finetune the model trained on the source domain.

